 # Exponential Decay Schedules
-Also called: Geometric LR Decay, Multiplicative LR Decay
 
 ## Overview
-Exponential decay schedules reduce the learning rate multiplicatively over training steps, providing a smooth, continuous transition from high initial exploration to fine-grained convergence. This family differs from [Linear Learning Rate Schedule](11850-linear-learning-rate-schedule.md) by applying relative reductions rather than absolute ones, and from [Cosine Decay Learning Rate Schedule](14118-cosine-decay-learning-rate-schedule.md) by avoiding the symmetric "slow-fast-slow" trajectory in favor of a monotonic decrease . It is primarily used in NeRF optimization to stabilize training when the model has converged to a coarse geometry but requires precise refinement of appearance and density fields.
+Exponential decay schedules reduce the learning rate multiplicatively over training steps, providing a smooth, continuous transition from high initial exploration to fine-grained convergence [G]. This family differs from [Linear Learning Rate Schedule](11850-linear-learning-rate-schedule.md) by applying relative reductions rather than absolute ones, and from [Cosine Decay Learning Rate Schedule](14118-cosine-decay-learning-rate-schedule.md) by avoiding the symmetric "slow-fast-slow" trajectory in favor of a monotonic decrease [G]. It is primarily used in NeRF optimization to stabilize training when the model has converged to a coarse geometry but requires precise refinement of appearance and density fields [G].
 
