 ## Background
-Exponential decay is a standard technique in optimization, widely adopted in early neural network training and retained in NeRF pipelines for its simplicity and effectiveness in fine-tuning . In the context of differentiable volume rendering, it addresses the problem of converging sparse input data by preventing large gradient updates once the model has established a coherent geometric prior .
